(
 'Clones a repository.'
 ''
 'Requires a URL of the repo to be cloned. If only <username>/<reponame> is specified, this defaults to'
 'GitHub. If you don''t specify <.git> at the end, it''s added for you.'
 ''
 'Note that in case you specify only <username>/<reponame>, an HTTP request will be performed. If you want'
 'to perform an SSH request instead, you can either use the full syntax:'
 '  git@github.com:<userid>/<reponame>'
 'or you just add a leading "@":'
 '  @<userid>/<reponame>'
 (,' ')
 'However, this defaults to GitHub, so in case you do not use GitHub, the syntax shortcut is not available.'
 ''
 'Note that there is no way to provide an SSH passphrase when called from Dyalog. So if you want to use'
 'SSH make sure that you do not specify a passphrase to encrypt your private key.'
 ''
 'By default, the user command acts on the current directory but asks for confirmation.'
 'You may specify a path via an optional second argument.'
 ''
 'By default all branches are cloned, but see -branch='
 ''
 '-branch=      Use this to clone only a specific branch'
 '-depth=<int>  Use this to specify the number of commits to be cloned'
 '-dry          If specified the "clone" command is returned without executing it'
 ''
 'For more information execute:'
 ']APLGit2.CloneRepo -???'
)
